 !!! Warning
     The `tradable_balance_ratio` setting applies to the current balance (free balance + tied up in trades). Therefore, assuming the starting balance of 1000, a configuration with `tradable_balance_ratio=0.99` will not guarantee that 10 currency units will always remain available on the exchange. For example, the free amount may reduce to 5 units if the total balance is reduced to 500 (either by a losing streak or by withdrawing balance).
 
+#### Limit exposure to a single underlying currency
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against, or backed by, the same underlying currency
+(for example a handful of BTC-margined futures, or several coins that are all quoted in the same
+stablecoin), a large adverse move in that one currency can hit several of your open trades at once,
+even though each trade looked fine in isolation.
+
+`max_currency_exposure` lets you cap the share of your tradable capital that may be committed at the
+same time to open trades sharing a pair's underlying (quote/settlement) currency. For example,
+`max_currency_exposure=0.5` ensures that no more than 50% of your tradable capital is ever committed to
+BTC-settled trades at once - regardless of how many individual BTC-settled pairs are open.
+
+When opening (or adding to) a trade would push the combined stake for that currency above the
+configured share, the stake amount is reduced to fit under the limit, the same way stake amounts are
+already adjusted for exchange or `stake_amount` limits; if there is no room left at all, the trade is
+not opened. This is enforced identically in live/dry-run and in backtesting.
+
+Defaults to `1` (100%), which disables the limit.
+
+!!! Note
+    This limit is evaluated in addition to `max_open_trades`, `stake_amount` and `tradable_balance_ratio` - it never increases the amount the bot is allowed to trade, only potentially reduces it further.
+
 #### Assign available Capital
 
 To fully utilize compounding profits when using multiple bots on the same exchange account, you'll want to limit each bot to a certain starting balance.
